    '- ESUM summarizes OUTSIDE-F history for patterns & responsiveness.',
    '- OR lines describe protected needs on other rota(s) within the planning horizon; treat OR.need as a capacity constraint (narrowly emitted only where headcount < need).',
    '',
    'CLASH & CONTINUITY MODEL:',
    '- HARD (absolute) blocks:',
    '  • Booked elsewhere (EH/EB) on the same date: reject.',
    '  • Night→Long day next day (from any rota via EH): reject.',
    '  • Unique-coverer for a protected OR cell: reject.',
    '  • 6-day streak cap counting EH + planned: reject.',
    '- SOFT (finite) steering:',
    '  • Potential clash penalty ONLY if the candidate is affiliated with the protected rota (≥1 shift there in last 14 days) AND OR.need>0.',
    '    - Regularity tiers (last 14 days): Rare=0–2, Occasional=3–7, Regular=8+.',
    '    - Rare-trending: if Rare=2 and both within last 4 days → stronger penalty than baseline Rare.',
    '    - Predictability alignment: if their DoW/shift pattern on that rota aligns with the target date/shift, increase penalty; if mismatch (e.g., usually Nights there but we need Long day), reduce penalty.',
    '  • No affiliation → no potential penalty even if OR.need>0.',
    '',
    'EVALUATION ORDER (engine-enforced):',
    '1) Hard screens (role/gender/availability/EB/EH/N→L/6-day/horizon).',
    '2) Potential clash penalty (affiliation-based, OR.need>0).',
    '3) Continuity & streak (prefer extending 4–5 same-shift blocks; fewer distinct staff).',
    '4) Availability evidence (declared ≫ pattern-based with confidence).',
    '5) Tie-breakers: recency/activity and ESUM weekday match.',
    '',
    'PRESENTATION:',
    '- Use "Long day" / "Night" in prose (not codes).',
